      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried PI3USB9201_USB_PATH_ON instead of PI3USB9201_SDP_HOST_MODE. That doesn\u0027t work because I get PI3USB9201_REG_HOST_STS_DEV_UNPLUG as soon as I set PI3USB9201_USB_PATH_ON, I assume because PI3USB9201_USB_PATH_ON doesn\u0027t support plug/unplug detection.\n\nI tested wake from S3 via USB2 keyboard and that works with PI3USB9201_SDP_HOST_MODE (and PI3USB9201_CDP_HOST_MODE, and PI3USB9201_USB_PATH_ON).\n\nThe datasheet says \"Support USB Switch Pass-through for Mouse/Keyboard Wake up\" under \"Host Mode - SDP/CDP/DCP\". I don\u0027t read that as meaning that wake up doesn\u0027t work in SDP mode, but I\u0027ve asked Diodes to check. I\u0027m also not sure if this is some USB wake up that is different from wake from S3: if so then I don\u0027t know how to test that.",
